**Corollary 4.4 (independent history kernels on the combined domain).**
For each $V\in\{S,B,M_J,T\}$ separately and $h,h'\in\mathcal C_{\mathrm{gc}}$,

$$
V(h)=V(h')\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad h=h'.
$$

Proof. S/B give $W$ by Lemma 3.3 and then history by Theorem 4.3. M
gives its basic selected data directly, then history by that theorem;
its full role selection is deterministic. T's canonical local patch
records reconstruct each actual successor from the common foundation
and their own IN bits, by CYCLE Lemma 5.4 and Lemma 2.6. The other
direction in each case is equality of the independently defined object
on the same history. This is a consumed extension of the existing
history-kernel method to the mode/general-target graph. It is not a
claim about $Q$ at all these cuts. ∎

